WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Looks perfect.

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.300
The checker on the live site: 25 out of 100.
"Very little selectable text was found."

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.000
0 words of selectable text.
Mohamed's CV is a picture. An ATS may misread it.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.800
Start from a CV built to be read.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.500
5 templates: Network & Cloud, Embedded & ECE, Mobile Apps,
Software Engineering, Business & Finance. Free, MIT licensed.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.500
No LaTeX skills needed. 3 ways to edit:
Overleaf, with AI, or locally.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.500
01 On Overleaf: click "Edit on Overleaf".
Free account, nothing to install.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:21.500
Change the text inside the { }, then Recompile.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.000
02 With AI: click "Copy for ChatGPT".

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.500
Paste it into ChatGPT, Gemini or Claude.
The prompt says: one page, no invented numbers.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.500
Read every line before you send it.
You will be asked about it in the interview.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.500
03 Already use LaTeX? Build it locally:
latexmk -pdf resume.tex

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.700
Check it again with the same checker.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.000
25 → 100. Mohamed's CV, rebuilt from a template.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Free, open source, no sign-up.
amrelsherif-eng.github.io/ats-resume-templates
